However, this solution has an exponential time complexity due to repeated calculations. A more efficient approach is using dynamic programming (memoization):

```python
def fib(n, memo={}):
    if n in memo:
        return memo[n]
    elif n <= 1:
        result = n
    else:
        result = fib(n-1) + fib(n-2)
        memo[n] = result
    return result
```

